            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "```suggestion\n      -- Since the actual connection establishment is done asynchronously, we cannot throw an error on failure,\n      -- therefore we treat the failure of the actual connection as a disconnection of our abstracted connection.\n      -- Furthermore, because we also allow writes before the actual connection is established,\n      -- this makes the underlying actual connection remain transparent to the user.\n      on_read(nil, nil)\n```\nI think doing it this way would be better, as it should make our abstraction for the connection more complete.\n\nCurrently, these two approaches are effectively equivalent due to the existing code. \nhttps://github.com/neovim/neovim/blob/c696bab8475a80aa49295b3c9e6d1a18d1332f0e/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/rpc.lua#L336-L339\nHowever, this method provides room for future users to customize how connections are handled when disconnected from a remote source.",
            "commit_id": "6451f84f14eb44f4f5a8f2990a7380ead509a403",
            "created_at": "2026-09-09T07:29:34Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -137,6 +137,7 @@ function TransportConnect:listen(on_read, on_exit)\n           vim.log.levels.WARN\n         )\n       end)\n+      self:terminate()",
